1
00:00:17,210 --> 00:01:10,401
这是我上次写在黑板上的内容，当时写错了。这是下周一（8号）截止的作业。现在我们回到正多面体。我们在 ℝ^3 中有与正多面体相关联的有限群，群 Gamma 将是SO(3) 的子群，即保持正多面体 S 不变的旋转。
So this is what I put up last time, which was mistaken. This is the homework due Monday the 8th. So let's go back to the regular solids. So we have the finite groups associated to the regular solids in ℝ^3, and the group Gamma is going to be a subgroup of SO(3), the rotations preserving a regular solid S.

2
00:01:10,401 --> 00:01:38,885
一共有五种正多面体：正四面体，正如我们所证明的，此时 Gamma 的阶为 12；我们将证明它同构于 A_4，作用是置换各个顶点，因为有 4 个顶点，所以这给出了 S_4 的一个子群，并且我们将证明它就是交错群。
So there are five regular solids: the tetrahedron, and Gamma is of order 12 in this case, as we showed; and we're going to show it is isomorphic to A_4, permuting the vertices, because there are four vertices, so that gives you a subgroup of S_4, and we're going to show it's the alternating group.

3
00:01:38,885 --> 00:01:45,272
上次我们讨论了正八面体，但事实证明，对于它的对偶多面体——立方体，你得到的 Gamma 是完全相同的。
Then last time we discussed the octahedron, but it turns out you get the same Gamma for the dual solid, which is called the cube.

4
00:01:45,272 --> 00:02:06,281
对于这两者，Gamma 的阶都是 24，今天我将向大家证明它同构于 S_4，作用是置换立方体的体对角线。我将向大家演示这是如何成立的。
Here, for both of these, Gamma is of order 24, and I'm going to show you today it is isomorphic to S_4, permuting diagonals of the cube. I'll show you how that works.

5
00:02:06,281 --> 00:02:20,520
上次我提到了有 20 个面的正二十面体，但今天我也要向大家展示正十二面体，它有 12 个面。
And last time I talked about the icosahedron, which has 20 faces, but today I'll show you also the dodecahedron, which has 12 faces.

6
00:02:20,520 --> 00:02:27,353
Gamma 的阶为 60，今天我就不证明它同构于 5 个字母上的交错群了——那相当棘手。
Gamma has order 60, and I won't prove today that it's the alternating group on five letters—that's quite tricky.

7
00:02:27,353 --> 00:02:35,348
它碰巧同构于 A_5，但它所置换的 5 个对象很难直接写出来。
It happens to be isomorphic to A_5, but what five things it permutes are hard to write down.

8
00:02:35,348 --> 00:02:53,527
但我会证明它是一个单群：没有非平凡正规子群。因此这是我们关于非交换单群的第一个例子。
But I will show it's a simple group: no non-trivial normal subgroups. So it's our first example of a non-abelian simple group.

9
00:02:53,527 --> 00:03:07,239
我们已知一些交换单群；事实上，唯一的交换单群就是素数阶循环群。
We have some abelian simple groups; in fact, the only abelian simple groups are the cyclic groups of order p.

10
00:03:10,310 --> 00:03:21,333
如果你有一个阶数不是素数的交换群，它就有非平凡子群，因此就有非平凡正规子群，所以不是单群。
If you have any abelian group whose order is not a prime, it has non-trivial subgroups and therefore non-trivial normal subgroups, so isn't simple.

11
00:03:21,333 --> 00:03:29,069
但如果它的阶是素数，那么任何子群要么是平凡群要么是整个群，因为任何元素的阶要么是该素数要么是 1，即 p 阶循环群。
But if it's of order a prime, then any subgroup is either the trivial group or the entire group, because any element has prime order or 1, cyclic of order p.

12
00:03:29,069 --> 00:03:34,565
所以唯一的交换单群——我们已经完全了解它们，它们对应于素数。
So the only abelian simple groups—we know them, they correspond to the prime numbers.

13
00:03:34,565 --> 00:03:46,360
而这是第一个非交换单群，稍后我会讲一点关于非交换单群的内容，但最小的一个阶为 60。
And this is the first non-abelian simple group, and I'll talk a little bit about non-abelian simple groups, but the first one is of order 60.

14
00:03:46,360 --> 00:04:10,250
好，我们先来看正四面体，因为上次我们证明了存在一个传递地置换顶点的群。在这种情况中，有 1 个单位元 e，有 8 个固定某个顶点的 3 阶旋转。
Okay, so let's go through the tetrahedron, because last time we proved that there was a group that permuted the vertices transitively. In this case, there are one element e, there are eight rotations of order 3 fixing a vertex.

15
00:04:10,250 --> 00:04:17,946
每个顶点都有一个小旋转群，你可以旋转 120 度或 240 度。
So each vertex has a little rotation group where you rotate either by 120 degrees or by 240 degrees.

16
00:04:17,946 --> 00:04:26,305
这两个给出了两个不同的 3 阶旋转，并且一共有 4 个顶点，所以一共有 8 个不同的保持正四面体不变的 3 阶旋转。
Those give two different rotations of order 3, and there are four vertices, so there are eight different rotations of order 3 preserving the tetrahedron.

17
00:04:26,305 --> 00:04:44,500
上次我说过还有 3 个2 阶旋转，它们在顶点上的作用是交换两对顶点。
And last time I said there are three rotations of order 2, which on the vertices switch pairs of vertices.

18
00:04:46,400 --> 00:04:58,570
例如作为置换它可能看起来像这样：不固定任何顶点，而是同时交换两对不同的顶点。
So for example, as a permutation it might look like this: doesn't fix anything, but it switches two different pairs of vertices.

19
00:04:58,570 --> 00:05:12,690
很容易向大家展示这一点，如果我手里拿着这个模型并举起来：我们要交换这两个顶点，这里的两个顶点会被交换，而这里的两个顶点也会被交换。
So it's easy to show you that, if I actually have the thing and I can hold it up: so we're going to switch these two vertices, and so the two vertices here are going to be switched, and the two vertices here are going to be switched.

20
00:05:12,690 --> 00:05:14,038
那么什么样的旋转能做到这点？
So what rotation does that?

21
00:05:14,038 --> 00:05:30,963
取旋转轴——旋转由其转轴决定——取穿过这条棱的轴，即你要交换的顶点所在的这条棱，以及对棱。穿过这条棱的中点与对棱的中点作一条直线，绕该轴旋转 180 度，就像这样。
You take the axis—a rotation is determined by its axis—you take the axis through this edge, the vertices you're going to switch here, and this edge. So you draw a line through the center of this edge and this edge, and you rotate 180 degrees around that axis, like that.

22
00:05:30,963 --> 00:05:38,223
你会注意到它交换了这两个顶点，且这两个顶点也互换了。
And you notice it switches these two vertices, and these two vertices go back.

23
00:05:38,223 --> 00:06:07,287
好，所以这是 180 度的 2 阶旋转，转轴是连接 1 和 2 的棱的中点  到连接 3 和 4 的棱的中点。
Okay, so it's a rotation of order 2, 180 degrees, and the axis is the midpoint of the edge connecting 1 and 2   to the midpoint of the edge connecting 3 and 4.

24
00:06:07,287 --> 00:06:24,749
对于任何两对顶点，你都可以穿过对棱的中点作轴。如果我取这两条棱，穿过这里和这里作轴，然后绕它旋转 180 度。
And for any pairs of vertices, you can draw the axis through the midpoint of the opposite edges. If I took these two, then I have these two, I draw the axis through here and here, and rotate 180 degrees around that.

25
00:06:24,749 --> 00:06:33,289
你必须手里拿着正四面体实际操作一下，就会看到有三对对棱中点可供使用。
So you have to actually do that with a tetrahedron in hand, and you'll see that there are three pairs of opposite midpoints that you can use.

26
00:06:33,289 --> 00:06:36,812
这给出了 3 个 2 阶元素，它们作为置换看起来像这样。
That gives you three elements of order 2, which as permutations look like this.

27
00:06:36,812 --> 00:06:44,780
现在是时候引入一套良好的置换记号了，因为我受够画箭头了——这不是标准记号。
Now it's time that we started introducing good notation for permutations, because I'm sick of doing this—this is not the standard notation.

28
00:06:44,780 --> 00:06:58,350
这个置换通常这样表示——我们将有专门的一节、整整一讲专门讲解如何在对称群中进行计算。让我们把记号规范下来。对于置换，你的表示方法就是追踪元素的去向。
This permutation would be denoted—and we're going to have a whole section, a whole lecture just on how to do computations in the symmetric group. Let's get our notation down right. What you do with a permutation, the way you notate it is you follow where elements go.

29
00:06:58,350 --> 00:07:15,635
因此它是这样的：我如下表示这个置换。我先写一个括号，然后写 1，接着写下 1 的去向：它变到 2。好，在 2 之后我接着写下2 的去向。
So this would go like this: I notate this permutation as follows. I'd start with a bracket, then I take 1, then the next thing I put down is where 1 goes: it goes to 2. Okay, now the next thing I put down after 2 is where 2 goes.

30
00:07:15,635 --> 00:07:30,714
如果它变回 1（在本例中确实如此），你就把括号闭合，这表示它把 1 变成 2，并且把括号里的最后一个数变回第一个数 1。然后我们还有 3 变到 4；
If it gets back to 1, which it does in this case, you close off the parenthesis like that, which means that this effectively takes 1 to 2, and it takes the last thing here back to the first thing, 1. And then I'd also have 3 going to 4;

31
00:07:30,714 --> 00:07:55,820
这就是我表示该置换的方式。好，我们再来表示 S_4 中的另一个置换。我们来表示固定 4、但让其余元素轮换的置换。好，它可以记为：(1 2 3)(4)。
that's how I'd notate that permutation. Okay, let's notate another permutation in S_4. Let's do the permutation that fixes 4, but that circles the others around. Okay, that would be notated as follows: (1 2 3)(4).

32
00:07:55,820 --> 00:08:07,302
它把 1 变到 2，把 2 变到 3，把 3 变回 1，把 4 变到自身。明白了吗？
It takes 1 to 2, it takes 2 to 3, it takes 3 back to 1, and it takes 4 to itself. Get the idea?

33
00:08:07,302 --> 00:08:15,840
再次强调，这里没有任何高深思想，这只是一种记法，免得把数字写两遍还画一堆箭头，对吧？
Again, there's no thought in this, it's just a way of writing down this thing without having to write the numbers twice and a bunch of arrows, okay?

34
00:08:15,840 --> 00:08:41,487
这种记号稍微更紧凑一些。  我们再看另一个置换，5 个元素的置换：1, 2, 3, 4, 5。来看这个置换：1 到 2，2 到 1，3 到 5，4 到 3，5 到 4。这是 5 个元素的一个很好的置换。
It's a little bit more compact as notation.   Let's do another permutation, let's do a permutation of five things: 1, 2, 3, 4, 5. Let's do this permutation: 1 to 2, 2 to 1, 3 to 5, 4 to 3, 5 to 4. That's a good permutation of five things.

35
00:08:41,487 --> 00:08:57,552
它可以记作：(1 2)，所以你有一个小的 (1 2)，2 变回 1，然后是 (3 5 4)：3 变到 5，5 变到 4，4变回 3。
It would be notated like this: (1 2), so you have a little (1 2), 2 goes back to 1, and then (3 5 4): 3 goes to 5, 5 goes to 4, 4 goes back to 3.

36
00:08:57,552 --> 00:09:02,525
好，所以从现在起我们就这样表示置换。
Okay, so from now on we're going to notate our permutations this way.

37
00:09:02,525 --> 00:09:17,330
特别是，这些 3 阶元素看起来像这样：(1 2 3)(4)，(13 2)(4)，因为这是固定元素 4 的两个旋转。
So in particular, these elements of order 3 look like this: (1 2 3)(4), (1 3 2)(4), because those are the two rotations that fix the element 4.

38
00:09:17,330 --> 00:09:40,895
然后我们还有像 (1 2 4)(3) 和 (14 2)(3)，接着还有 (1 3 4)(2) 和 (1 4 3)(2)，再接着还有 (2 3 4)(1) 和 (2 43)(1)。
And then I'd have things like (1 2 4)(3) and (1 4 2)(3), and then I'd have (1 3 4)(2) and (1 4 3)(2), and then I'd have (2 3 4)(1) and (2 4 3)(1).

39
00:09:40,895 --> 00:09:49,358
这些就是正四面体群中全部 8 个 3 阶置换。
Those would be my eight permutations of order 3 in this group of the tetrahedron.

40
00:09:49,358 --> 00:10:03,650
而其余 2 阶元素：我有这一个 (1 2)(3 4)；有这一个(1 3)(2 4)，那意味着交换顶点 1 和 3 且交换顶点 2 和 4；最后还有 (1 4)(2 3)。
And the other elements of order 2: I'd have this one, (1 2)(3 4); I'd have this one, (1 3)(2 4), that would mean switching vertices 1 and 3 and switching vertices 2 and 4; and then finally I'd have (1 4)(2 3).

41
00:10:03,650 --> 00:10:19,586
对，最后单位元可以写成 (1)(2)(3)(4)：把 1 变到自身、2 到自身、3 到自身、4 到自身。这样把记号确定下来够清楚了吗？
Right, and then finally this element would be written (1)(2)(3)(4): takes 1 to itself, 2 to itself, 3 to itself, and 4 to itself. Is this enough to get the notation settled?

42
00:10:19,586 --> 00:10:23,113
我们将在对称群中进行很多计算，但记号就是这样。
We're going to do a lot of computations in the symmetric group, but that's it.

43
00:10:23,113 --> 00:10:29,000
现在，这个群之所以是 4 个字母上的交错群，是因为：首先，我们上次证明了它的阶为 12。
Now the reason that this is the alternating group on four letters is: first of all, we proved last time that it has order 12.

44
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:37,850
你可以验证所有这些置换若视作置换矩阵，行列式全都是 1。所以它们全都落在交错群中。
You can check that all of these permutations have determinant 1 if you think of them as permutation matrices. So they're all in the alternating group.

45
00:10:37,850 --> 00:10:53,174
因此无论这是什么，它都是交错群的子群，并且它们阶数相同，所以它同构于交错群。好，我们来看下一个。上次我们讲了正八面体；这次我换成立方体来做。
So whatever this is, it's a subgroup of the alternating group, and it has the same order, therefore it's isomorphic to the alternating group. Okay, let's do this one. Last time we did the octahedron; I'll do it for the cube this time.

46
00:10:53,174 --> 00:11:06,244
论证非常类似：立方体有 8 个顶点，有 6 个面——是的，6 个面——并且有 1, 2, 3, 4——抱歉，12 条棱，谢谢。
It's a similar argument: the cube has 8 vertices, and has 6 faces—it has, yes, 6 faces—and has 1, 2, 3, 4—pardon, 12 edges, thank you.

47
00:11:06,244 --> 00:11:26,570
顶点的稳定子群 Gamma_v，即固定一个顶点的元素：如果我固定一个顶点并取穿过该顶点的轴……抱歉，我们来固定一个面，这更容易看清楚原因。
The stabilizer of a vertex, Gamma_v, the things fixing a vertex: well, if I fix a vertex and I take the axis through that vertex... sorry, let's fix a face, it's easier, it's easier to see why.

48
00:11:26,570 --> 00:11:39,440
假设我想固定这个红色的面：我取穿过该面的中心与对面的中心的转轴，绕该轴有 4 阶旋转，对吧？就是这样，固定一个面的元素。
Suppose I want to fix this red face: I take the axis through the midpoint of that face and the opposite face, and I have the rotations of order 4 around that axis, right? So that's it, the fixer of a face.

49
00:11:39,440 --> 00:11:53,618
我们看这种情况：固定一个面的 Gamma_F 阶为 4，而 4 乘以 6——因为群传递地置换各个面，我可以绕这里旋转把这四个面互相轮换，
Let's do that case: Gamma of a face is of order 4, and 4 times 6—because it permutes the faces transitively, I can take these four faces to themselves by rotating around here,

50
00:11:53,618 --> 00:12:08,446
如果我想把红色的面变到例如蓝色的面，我取穿过这些面的轴并像这样旋转 90 度，从而可以传递地置换各个面。这证明了该群的阶为 24。
and if I want to take the red face to say the blue face, I take the axis through these faces and I rotate a quarter turn like that, and so I can permute the faces transitively. So that shows the group has order 24.

51
00:12:08,446 --> 00:12:13,435
现在为了证明它是 S_4 的子群，我必须给出它所置换的 4 个对象。
Now to show that it's a subgroup of S_4, I have to give four things that it permutes.

52
00:12:13,435 --> 00:12:21,805
但我并没有 4 个顶点，也没有4 个面，也没有像正四面体那样的 4 条棱，因此它置换哪 4 个对象并不明显。
And I don't have four vertices, and I don't have four faces, and I don't have four edges like I did for the tetrahedron, so it's not obvious what four things it permutes.

53
00:12:21,805 --> 00:12:32,218
然而，如果它把立方体变到自身，它就会置换连接相对顶点的体对角线。一共有 4 条这样的体对角线，因为有 8 个顶点，对吧？
However, if it takes the cube to itself, it permutes the diagonals that connect opposite vertices. And there are four such diagonals, because there are eight vertices, right?

54
00:12:32,218 --> 00:12:42,175
所以它把这些对角线变到自身，从而给出了 4 个对象的置换，因为它把顶点变到顶点，保持每个顶点及其相对顶点的对应关系。
So it takes those diagonals to themselves, so it gives a permutation of four things, because it takes the vertices to themselves, so it preserves a vertex and its opposite vertex.

55
00:12:42,175 --> 00:12:53,129
这就是置换体对角线；这表明它是 S_4 的子群。但它们的阶相同，所以我不需要做任何繁杂计算：它同构于 S_4。
So this is permuting the diagonals; that gives us this as a subgroup of S_4. But they have the same order, so I don't have to do any computations: they're isomorphic to S_4.

56
00:12:53,129 --> 00:13:13,786
至于正二十面体，是的——每当有一个把立方体变到自身的运动，它把顶点变到顶点，因此它把穿过相对顶点的直线变到穿过相对顶点的直线，
And for the icosahedron, yeah— anytime I have a motion that takes the cube to itself, right, it takes the vertices to themselves, so it takes the lines through opposite vertices to lines through opposite vertices,

57
00:13:13,786 --> 00:13:21,579
因为该对跖关系被保持；而一共有 4 条这样的直线，因此立方体的任何运动都会置换它们。
because it preserves the relation; and there are four such lines, so they are permuted whenever I have a motion of the cube.

58
00:13:21,579 --> 00:13:39,369
反之，如果我知道该置换是什么，我就知道顶点变到了哪里，或者至少知道各对相对顶点变到了哪里，但事实上顶点具体的去向决定了该旋转；这给出了从 Gamma 到 S_4 的映射。它们的阶相同，所以它们同构。
Conversely, if I know what that permutation is, I know where the vertices have gone, or at least where the pairs of opposite vertices are gone, but in fact where the vertices have gone, and that becomes the rotation; and that gives me a map from Gamma into S_4. They have the same order, they're isomorphic.

59
00:13:39,369 --> 00:13:56,479
今天处理正二十面体：对我来说做模型比较容易——正二十面体每个面是三角形，每个顶点周围有 5 个三角形，而这个模型的面是五边形，每个顶点周围有 3 个五边形……啊对了，这是正十二面体，我道个歉！
Doing today for the icosahedron: it was easier for me to build—so the icosahedron, instead of the faces being triangles and having five triangles around a given vertex, the faces are pentagons and you have three pentagons... oh yeah, this is a dodecahedron, I apologize!

60
00:13:56,479 --> 00:14:14,581
上次我试图搭一个正二十面体，我差点累死，因为你得在一个顶点周围拼 5 个三角形。而这里每个顶点周围是 3 个五边形，对吧？所以有了这个模型：正十二面体有 12 个面，现在是五边形。
The last time I tried to build an icosahedron and I almost died, because yeah, you have to put five triangles around a vertex. So here's three pentagons around each vertex, right? So you have this thing: the dodecahedron has 12 faces, which are now pentagons.

61
00:14:14,581 --> 00:14:23,792
请注意，立方体的面是正方形，而不是我们在正八面体中见到的三角形。
Notice that in the cube, instead of having faces that were triangles which we had for the octahedron, we have faces which are squares.

62
00:14:23,792 --> 00:14:43,698
而这里我们有 12 个五边形的面；顶点的数量——抱歉，1, 2, 3, 4……是的，12 个面，顶点的数量是多少？
So here we have 12 faces that are pentagons; we have the number of vertices—sorry, 1, 2, 3, 4... yeah, the 12 faces, the number of vertices is what?

63
00:14:43,698 --> 00:14:50,110
20 个顶点，我刚才忘了具体数量……没错，20 个顶点，谢谢！并且同样有 30 条棱。
20 vertices, I forget how many... that's it, 20 vertices, thank you! And again, 30 edges.

64
00:14:50,110 --> 00:14:55,328
现在同样地，为了求出这里的群，我们要求出一个面的稳定子群。
Now again, to figure out the group here, we'll figure out the stabilizer of a face.

65
00:14:55,328 --> 00:15:12,160
如果要固定一个面，我取穿过该面以及穿过对面的旋转轴，然后我可以绕转轴旋转五分之一周（72度），从而固定这个面，同时也固定底部的对面。
Well, if I want to stabilize a face, I take the axis of rotation through the face and through the opposite face, and then I can rotate around 1/5 of the circle and stabilize this face, and it also stabilizes this face underneath.

66
00:15:12,160 --> 00:15:28,182
好，所以面的稳定子群的阶为 5，是 5 阶循环群，而 12 乘以 5 等于 60，这就是该群的阶。
Okay, and so our stabilizer of the face turns out to have order 5, cyclic of order 5, and 12 times 5 is 60, and that's the order of the group.

67
00:15:28,182 --> 00:15:39,680
我无法直接向大家展示它同构于 A_5，因为要给出该群中被 A_5 保持不变的对象相当复杂，要给出保持不变的 5 个对象。
I can't show you that it's isomorphic to A_5, because to give you something that's preserved by A_5 in this group is quite complicated, to give you five objects that are preserved.

68
00:15:39,680 --> 00:15:49,615
Artin 的书里给出了一个例子：如果你在正十二面体内内接立方体，里面有 5 个立方体在旋转作用下彼此互换。
Artin gives an example: if you inscribe cubes inside of a dodecahedron, there are five cubes inside of this that are taken to each other by rotations.

69
00:15:49,615 --> 00:15:51,743
我连画都不想尝试画——请大家去看教材。
I don't want to even try to draw that—take a look at the book.

70
00:15:51,743 --> 00:16:00,222
我先请大家姑且相信它是 A_5；我们眼下不需要这个事实。我将向大家证明的是，它是一个非交换单群。
I'll just ask you to believe for the moment that it's A_5; we don't need that at the moment. What I'm going to show you is that it's a non-abelian simple group.

71
00:16:00,222 --> 00:16:05,259
为了做到这一点，我们必须弄清楚它的共轭类有哪些，好吗？
So to do that, we have to figure out what are the conjugacy classes, okay?

72
00:16:05,259 --> 00:16:13,877
现在这 12 个面，我断言，给出了 6 个 5 阶循环子群。
Now the 12 faces, I claim, give me six cyclic subgroups of order 5.

73
00:16:13,877 --> 00:16:20,190
所以我们现在要推导出 Gamma 中的各个共轭类。
So we're now going to work out the conjugacy classes in Gamma.

74
00:16:25,110 --> 00:16:42,088
这些面给出了 6 个同构于 ℤ/5ℤ 的子群。原因在于每一对相对的面对应于同一个旋转子群。
So the faces give six subgroups isomorphic to ℤ/5ℤ. The reason is that you get the same subgroup of rotations for each pair of opposite faces.

75
00:16:42,088 --> 00:16:52,527
绕这里有 5 个旋转，绕对面也是这 5 个旋转，对吧？所以 12 个面给出了 6 对相对面，即 6 个5 阶子群。
So I have five rotations around here, and then I have five rotations around here, right? So the 12 faces give six pairs of opposite faces, six subgroups of order 5.

76
00:16:52,527 --> 00:17:04,893
这 6 个不同的子群：它们相交的唯一可能就是单位元，因为两个不同子群的交集必然同时是两者的子群。
So the six different subgroups: the only way those subgroups can intersect is in the identity, because the intersection of two distinct subgroups would be a subgroup of both.

77
00:17:04,893 --> 00:17:13,136
但 5 阶循环群的子群要么是全群要么是单位元，所以除了单位元以外它们没有任何交集。
But a subgroup of a cyclic group of order 5 is either the whole group or the identity element, so they have no intersection but the identity.

78
00:17:13,136 --> 00:17:42,768
所以这 6 个 5 阶子群大概长成这样，并且在每一个子群中你得到 4 个5 阶元素，即群里的非单位元，它们是群里互不相同的元素。因此这给出了 24 个 5 阶元素。好，下一步：正如我说过的，我们有30 条棱。
So these six subgroups of order 5 sort of look like this, and you get in each one four elements of order 5, the non-identity elements in the group, and they're distinct elements in the group. So that gives 24 elements of order 5. Okay, next step: we have, as I said, 30 edges.

79
00:17:42,768 --> 00:18:00,834
每条棱都有一条对棱，如果你取穿过该棱中点的转轴，就像我们对正四面体所做的那样，你可以绕该轴旋转 180 度并保持正十二面体不变。所以这是 2 阶元素，对吧？
Now if you have an edge, it has an opposite edge, and if you take the axis through the midpoint of that edge, just like we did for the tetrahedron, you can rotate 180 degrees around that axis and preserve the dodecahedron. So that's an element of order 2, right?

80
00:18:00,834 --> 00:18:26,630
因此30 条棱给出了 15 个同构于 ℤ/2ℤ 的不同子群，因为每对对棱确定同一个子群。同样地，这些是不同的子群；它们仅在单位元处相交。
So you have 30 edges giving 15 different subgroups isomorphic to ℤ/2ℤ, because each pair of opposite edges determines the same subgroup. And again, those are distinct groups; they only intersect in the identity.

81
00:18:26,630 --> 00:18:33,730
在 2 阶子群中，只有 1 个非平凡元素，因此你得到 15 个2 阶元素。
In a subgroup of order 2, you only have one non-trivial element, so you get 15 elements of order 2.

82
00:18:35,760 --> 00:18:47,220
现在我们来看顶点：如果你取一对相对的顶点，你可以旋转 120 度或 240 度。
And now when we go to the vertices: if you take a pair of opposite vertices, you can rotate by 120 or 240 degrees.

83
00:18:47,220 --> 00:18:53,242
你有3 阶旋转，因为从每个顶点引出 3 条棱。
You have rotations of order 3, because you have three things coming out of the vertex.

84
00:18:53,242 --> 00:19:17,130
同样地，20 个顶点给出了 10 个同构于ℤ/3ℤ 的不同子群，每个子群给出 2 个非平凡的 3 阶元素，所以我们得到 20 个 3 阶元素。
So again, the 20 vertices give 10 different subgroups isomorphic to ℤ/3ℤ, and each one gives two non-trivial elements of order 3, so we get 20 elements of order 3.

85
00:19:17,130 --> 00:19:24,945
这样我们就有了单位元，然后有了所有这些元素。这是否耗尽了整个群？
And so we have the identity element, and then we have all of these elements. Does that exhaust the group?

86
00:19:24,945 --> 00:19:35,140
我们来加一下：这里有 39 个元素，再加上 20 个得到 59 个元素，加上单位元，正好是 60 个元素。这就是整个群！
Well, let's add it up: here we get 39 elements, then we get 20 more, 59 elements, plus the identity, that gives us 60 elements. That's the group!

87
00:19:35,140 --> 00:19:52,469
所以群中的任何元素，要么是固定一对对棱的 2 阶元素，要么是固定一对相对顶点的 3 阶元素，要么是固定一对相对面的 5 阶元素。好，到目前为止一切顺利。
So anything in the group is either an element of order 2 which fixes a pair of opposite edges, an element of order 3 which fixes a pair of opposite vertices, or an element of order 5 which fixes a pair of opposite faces. Okay, so far so good.

88
00:19:52,469 --> 00:20:14,098
是的，我刚才的意思是：我在 G 内部画出这 6 个不同的子群。这是 G；这是固定一对相对面的稳定子群。
Yeah, what I meant was this: I'm drawing the six different subgroups inside of G. Here's G; here is a stabilizer of a pair of opposite faces.

89
00:20:14,098 --> 00:20:20,340
现在的断言是，这 6 个不同子群的交集仅仅是单位元。
Now the claim is that the intersection of those six different groups is just the identity element.

90
00:20:20,340 --> 00:20:30,122
不可能有其中任何两个群相交出多于单位元的元素，原因在于这两个群的交集必然是其中之一的子群。
You can't have any of those two groups intersecting in more than the identity element, and the reason is that the intersection of those two groups would be a subgroup of one of them.

91
00:20:30,122 --> 00:20:42,189
但这是一个素数阶单群，所以它的子群只有全群或平凡群。如果交集是全群，那就意味着这两个子群相同。
But this is a simple group because it has prime order, so its only subgroups are the whole group or itself. So if the intersection were all of it, it would mean these two things were the same.

92
00:20:42,189 --> 00:20:48,366
但是固定这一对相对面的稳定子群与固定另一对相对面的稳定子群并不是同一个群；它们的作用完全不同！
But the stabilizer of this pair of opposite faces is not the same group as the stabilizer of this pair of opposite faces; they do different things!

93
00:20:48,366 --> 00:20:52,248
我的意思是，这个固定这个面和这个面，而那个固定这个面和这个面。
I mean, this one fixes this face and this face, and this one fixes this face and this face.

94
00:20:52,248 --> 00:21:00,623
所以它们——所以它们不是同一个群，因此交集只有单位元。所以这包含 5 个元素；给出 4 个 5 阶元素。
So they have—so they're not the same group, so they have no intersection. So therefore there are five elements in this; they give four elements of order 5.

95
00:21:00,623 --> 00:21:10,747
这些元素与这 4 个 5 阶元素互不相同，也与那 4 个元素互不相同。所以总数是 24 个，即 6 乘以 4，明白吗？
Those are distinct from these four elements of order 5, which are distinct from these four elements. So the total number is 24, 6 times 4, okay?

96
00:21:10,747 --> 00:21:15,737
你不需要对 2 阶子群做同样的说明，因为如果它们不相交，显然只有 1 个非平凡元素，对吧？
You don't have to do that for a subgroup of order 2, because if they don't intersect, I mean it's just... right?

97
00:21:15,737 --> 00:21:30,267
而对于3 阶元素，我们有 10 个不同的子群分支，不管 10 个画出来是什么样，每个包含 2 个 3 阶元素。所以这 20 个就是 10 乘以 2，好吗？
And for elements of order 3, we'd have 10 different things going off, whatever 10 looks like, and each one contains two elements of order 3. So this 20 is 10 times 2, okay?

98
00:21:30,267 --> 00:21:56,035
现在我们把这写下来。所以我们将这 60——因为我们要分析为什么这个群是单群——我们将这 60 写成 1 个 1 阶元素、15 个 2 阶元素、20 个 3 阶元素、24 个 5 阶元素。
Now let's write that down. So we have this 60—because we're going to analyze why this group is simple—we have this 60 written as one element of order 1, 15 elements of order 2, 20 elements of order 3, 24 elements of order 5.

99
00:21:56,035 --> 00:22:11,029
现在有一种可能性，你首先可能会猜测的是：2 阶元素不可能与 3 阶元素共轭，对吧？共轭元素必然具有相同的阶。
Now one possibility, the first thing you might guess is: now you can't have an element of order 2 conjugate to an element of order 3, right? Conjugate elements have the same order.

100
00:22:22,050 --> 00:22:38,000
这个结论成立的原因（你们在期中考试中做过），在于如果你有一个与 g 共轭的元素，设 g'等于 h g h^{-1}，且 g^m 等于单位元，
The reason that that is true, which you saw on the exam, is that if you have an element which is conjugate to g, say g' is equal to h g h^{-1}, and g^m is equal to the identity element,

101
00:22:38,000 --> 00:23:08,873
那么如果我取 g'^m 并将其写为 (h g h^{-1})(h g h^{-1}) 一直乘 m 次——这里一共有 m 项——  那么我就可以把中间的 h 和 h^{-1}全部对消掉，
then if I take g'^m and I write it as (h g h^{-1})(h g h^{-1}) all the way down m times—this is m times—   then I can cancel the h and the h^{-1} all through this to get h g^m h^{-1},

102
00:23:08,873 --> 00:23:24,574
得到 h g^m h^{-1}，而 g^m 是单位元，所以这等于 h h^{-1}，即单位元，这表明 g' 的 m 次幂也是单位元。但这证明了 g' 的阶小于或等于 g的阶。
and g^m is the identity, so this is just h h^{-1}, which is just the identity, which shows that the m-th power of g' is the identity. But that shows the order of g' is less than or equal to the order of g.

103
00:23:24,574 --> 00:23:32,075
然后你做反向论证，证明 g 的阶小于或等于 g' 的阶，所以它们相等。
But then you do the converse, and you show the order of g is less than or equal to the order of g', so they're equal.

104
00:23:32,075 --> 00:23:34,659
因此共轭元素具有相同的阶。
So conjugate elements have the same order.

105
00:23:34,659 --> 00:23:48,000
所以 G 中的共轭类必须……嗯，这是共轭类，你必须有由这些元素构成的共轭类……你知道，这可能会分解成不同的共轭类，
Therefore, the conjugacy classes in G have to be... well, this is a conjugacy class, you have to have a conjugacy class made up of the elements of... you know, this could break into different conjugacy classes,

106
00:23:48,000 --> 00:24:00,330
但这些元素拆分成的共轭类与那些共轭类互不相干，等等。有时在群中你很幸运，阶数完全决定了共轭类。
but these things have to break up into conjugacy classes that have nothing to do with these conjugacy classes, etc. Now sometimes in a group you get lucky, and the order determines the conjugacy class.

107
00:24:00,330 --> 00:24:17,139
例如，在 3 个字母上的对称群中就是如此：我们看到有 6 个元素，其中有 3 个 2 阶元素、2 个3 阶元素。
So for example, that can happen for example in the symmetric group on three letters: we saw we had six elements, we had three elements of order 2, two elements of order 3.

108
00:24:17,139 --> 00:24:23,617
所有 2 阶元素全都是共轭的；所有 3 阶元素也全都是共轭的，所以结论成立：共轭性完全由阶数决定。
The elements of order 2 were all conjugate; the elements of order 3 were all conjugate, so that did it: conjugacy was determined by the order.

109
00:24:23,617 --> 00:24:29,370
那么在这个群中，共轭类是否也可能仅仅由阶数决定？
Now is it possible that the conjugacy classes inside of this group are just determined by the orders?

110
00:24:29,370 --> 00:24:41,890
这是否可能就是该群的类方程？就像之前那个群，6 等于 1 加 2 加 3，分解为各个共轭类的阶？
Is it possible that this is the class equation for the group, like the previous one, you know, 6 is equal to 1 plus 2 plus 3 that broke down into conjugacy classes?

111
00:24:41,890 --> 00:24:49,892
是否可能恰好有 4 个共轭类：单位元、全体 2 阶元素、全体 3 阶元素，以及全体5 阶元素？
Could there be four conjugacy classes: the identity element, all the elements of order 2, all the elements of order 3, and all the elements of order 5?

112
00:24:49,892 --> 00:24:52,010
这可能吗？
Is that possible?

113
00:24:53,520 --> 00:24:57,687
不，这不可能。为什么？
No, it is not possible. Why?

114
00:24:57,687 --> 00:25:35,530
因为 G 的共轭类的元素个数等于 G 的阶除以该元素中心化子的阶（上次讲过），所以它必须整除 G 的阶。  但这里出现了一个矛盾：即 15 整除 60，20 整除 60，但 24 不能整除 60！
Because the order of a conjugacy class of G is equal to the order of G divided by the order of the centralizer of the element from last time, so it must divide the order of G.   And there's a problem here: namely, 15 divides 60, 20 divides 60, but 24 does not divide 60!

115
00:25:35,530 --> 00:26:08,370
所以全体 2 阶元素有可能落在同一个共轭类中，全体 3 阶元素也有可能落在同一个共轭类中，但这部分必须至少分成两个类，因为 24 不能整除 60。  全体 5 阶元素并不全都共轭！
So it's possible that all the elements of order 2 are in one conjugacy class, it's possible that all the elements of order 3 are in one conjugacy class, but this has to be at least two classes, because 24 doesn't divide 60.   The elements of order 5 are not all conjugate!

116
00:26:08,370 --> 00:26:09,863
那么实际情况是怎样的？
Now what happens?

117
00:26:09,863 --> 00:26:26,540
我将在几何上向大家展示，这非常优美，是可能出现的最简单情况：在类方程中，这是一个共轭类，这是一个共轭类，这是一个共轭类，而这部分拆分成两个共轭类。
I'm going to show you that geometrically it's totally cool, it's the simplest thing possible: given the class equation, this is a conjugacy class, this is a conjugacy class, this is a conjugacy class, and this breaks up into two conjugacy classes.

118
00:26:26,540 --> 00:26:48,774
一共有两个由 5 阶元素构成的共轭类，我现在就向大家展示它们。我们首先证明全体 2 阶元素全都是共轭的。我们记得 2 阶元素来自穿过对棱中点的轴并旋转 180 度。
There are two conjugacy classes of elements of order 5, and I'm going to show them to you here. Let's first prove that the elements of order 2 are all conjugate. So the elements of order 2, we remember, come from taking the midpoints through opposite edges and rotating 180 degrees.

119
00:26:48,774 --> 00:27:07,020
现在假设我有一个 2 阶元素，你给我另一个 2 阶元素，对应这条棱和那条棱，你想把绕这条棱旋转 180 度共轭变换到绕那条棱旋转 180 度。
Now suppose I had one element of order 2, and you gave me another element of order 2, maybe this edge and this edge, and you wanted to conjugate the rotation around this edge of 180 degrees to the rotation around this edge of 180 degrees.

120
00:27:07,020 --> 00:27:20,640
你觉得应该怎么做？记住这些是固定棱的旋转，对吧？棱是如何被群置换的？群在棱上的作用是传递的！
How do you imagine you do that? Remember these are the things fixing an edge, right? And the edges are permuted how? By the group transitively!

121
00:27:20,640 --> 00:27:37,150
因此，如果我能在群中找到一个把这条棱变到那条棱的元素（我确实能找到），很自然地，那个元素就会把固定这条棱的旋转共轭变换为固定那条棱的旋转。事实确实如此；你需要验证这一点。
So if I could find an element in the group that took this edge to this edge—and I can—it seems reasonable that that element would conjugate the rotation fixing this edge to the rotation fixing this edge. And in fact that happens; you have to check that.

122
00:27:37,150 --> 00:27:59,674
所以这些元素全都是共轭的，  由传递地置换各条棱的元素共轭相连。我来给大家写下来。
So these are all conjugate,   all conjugate by elements permuting the edges transitively. I'm going to write that out for you.

123
00:27:59,674 --> 00:28:07,190
我们写在这里：为什么它们是共轭的？
So here let's write it out: why is that conjugate?

124
00:28:15,320 --> 00:28:41,850
设 g^2 = e 是固定一对对棱的元素——我们称这对对棱为，比方说 1 和 2：对棱1 和 2，好吗？
Say g^2 is equal to the identity is an element fixing a pair of edges—we'll call opposite edges, I don't know, we'll call it 1, 2, something like that: opposite edges 1 and 2, okay?

125
00:28:41,850 --> 00:28:56,982
我们有另一对对棱 3 和 4；g' 是固定这对对棱的元素，这很关键。
And we have another pair of opposite edges, 3 and 4; g' is the element fixing the pair of edges, the important edges.

126
00:29:00,097 --> 00:29:11,741
好，设 G 中的 h 把棱 1 变到棱 3。我们知道可以做到这一点，因为群传递地置换各个棱。
Okay, let h in G take the edge 1 to the edge 3. We know we can do that because the group permutes the edges transitively.

127
00:29:11,741 --> 00:29:24,384
例如，这些棱碰巧都汇交在这个顶点周围，我只需取五分之一周的旋转就能把这些棱互变。但即使是任何其他棱，任意两对棱都可以通过某个旋转互相变换。
For example, these edges happen to be centered around this vertex, so I just take the rotation of 1/5 the circle that takes those edges. But even any other, any pair of edges can be taken one to another by some rotation.

128
00:29:24,384 --> 00:29:33,543
于是找到一个把棱 1 变到棱 3 的 h，那么它也会把棱 2 变到棱 4，因为它保持正十二面体不变。
So find an h that takes the edge 1 to the edge 3, then it takes the edge 2 to the edge 4, because it preserves the dodecahedron.

129
00:29:33,543 --> 00:29:38,789
因此一旦我知道一条棱变到哪里，我就知道其对棱变到哪里：相对关系保持不变，对吧？
So once I know where an edge goes, I know where its opposite edge goes: opposite is preserved, okay?

130
00:29:38,789 --> 00:30:05,150
然后我断言——希望我没写反——g' 等于 h g h^{-1}。我们来验证一下！我们必须验证它固定棱 3 和棱 4。
And then I claim—let's hope I get this right—that g' is equal to h g h^{-1}, I believe. Let's check! Well, we have to see that it fixes the edges 3 and 4.

131
00:30:05,150 --> 00:30:30,887
我们从这里开始，将它作用于棱 3：h把棱 1 变到棱 3，所以 h^{-1} 把棱 3 变到棱 1。g 固定棱 1，所以结果是 h(1)，而 h 把 1 变回棱 3。所以这个元素固定棱 3；它同样固定棱4。
So let's start, let's apply this to the edge 3: h takes the edge 1 to the edge 3, so h^{-1} takes the edge 3 to the edge 1. g fixes the edge 1, so it's h of 1, and h takes 1 back to the edge 3. So this element fixes the edge 3; it also fixes the edge 4.

132
00:30:30,887 --> 00:30:39,123
而固定棱 3 和 4 的 2 阶元素是唯一的，那正是我们的元素 g'。所以这就是我们的共轭关系。
And there's a unique element of order 2 that fixes the edges 3 and 4, which is our element g'. So here's our conjugation.

133
00:30:39,123 --> 00:30:49,685
好，现在你可能会问，为什么这不能证明全体 5 阶元素全都共轭，或者全体3 阶元素全都共轭呢？
Okay, now you'd say, well, why doesn't that prove that all these elements of order 5 are conjugate, or all these elements of order 3 are conjugate?

134
00:30:49,685 --> 00:30:57,946
因为我能传递地置换各个面，也能传递地置换各个顶点；为什么这不能将所有这些元素彼此置换呢？
Because I can permute the faces transitively, and I can permute the vertices transitively; why doesn't that permute all these elements one to another?

135
00:30:57,946 --> 00:31:28,177
刚才我对棱的固定元素给出的论证，能够证明这 6 个子群在 Gamma 内部全都是共轭的，同样地这 10 个子群在 Gamma 中也全都是共轭的。
Well, the same argument that I just gave you for the fixers of edges will show you that these six subgroups are all conjugate inside of Gamma, and likewise these 10 subgroups are conjugate in Gamma.

136
00:31:28,177 --> 00:31:50,040
因为如果我想把固定这两个顶点的 3 阶子群共轭变换到固定那两个顶点的子群，我只需取一个把这个顶点变到那个顶点的变换即可。听起来不错吧？但这并不意味着各个元素也是共轭的！
Because if I want to conjugate the subgroup fixing this vertex and this vertex, this subgroup of order 3 into the subgroup fixing this vertex and this vertex, I just take a transformation that takes this vertex to this vertex. Sound good? But that doesn't imply that the elements are!

137
00:31:50,040 --> 00:31:58,150
这 4 个元素作为一个整体与那 4 个元素共轭，但我们不知道是否能把这里的任意元素变到那里的任意元素。
All these four elements are conjugate to those four elements in some order, but we don't know that I can take any element here to any element there.

138
00:31:58,150 --> 00:32:08,958
2 阶群的特殊之处在于，一旦子群共轭，非平凡元素就必然共轭；但在 5 阶群或 3 阶群中，这并不直接成立。
What's peculiar about a group of order 2 is that once the subgroups are conjugate, the non-trivial elements are conjugate; but in a group of order 5 or a group of order 3, that doesn't follow.

139
00:32:08,958 --> 00:32:41,216
然而事实证明，不仅这些3 阶子群彼此共轭，而且你可以把该子群中的任意元素变到另一个子群中的任意元素，因此这 20 个 3 阶元素实际上全都是共轭的，我必须向大家证明这一点。我们来看看能否做到，是的。我们来看：
Now it turns out that not only are these subgroups of order 3 conjugate, but you can take any element in this subgroup to any element in this subgroup, so that these 20 elements of order 3 are actually conjugate, and I have to prove that to you. Let's see if I can do that, yeah. Let's see: we're going to take this group that does

140
00:32:41,216 --> 00:33:09,169
我们取绕该顶点顺时针旋转的 3 阶群。如果你取一个3 阶元素……关键在于——明白了，明白了：你实际上可以构造一个像这样把这个顶点变到对顶点的变换，如果你用它来做共轭，它就会置换子群中的两个元素。
a clockwise rotation around this vertex of order 3. So if you take one element of order 3... yeah, the point is—got it, got it: you can actually make a transformation that takes this vertex into this vertex like that, and if you conjugate by that, it conjugates around the two elements in the subgroup.

141
00:33:09,169 --> 00:33:23,594
主要是，只要我证明这个元素与它的逆元共轭——并且我知道它与该子群中的某个元素共轭——但另一方面，子群中的这两个元素是共轭的，不是通过子群内部的元素共轭，而是通过另一个元素。
Mainly, as long as I prove that this element is conjugate to this element—and I know it's conjugate to something in this group—but on the other hand, each pair of elements in the subgroup is conjugate not by an element in the subgroup, but by a different element.

142
00:33:23,594 --> 00:33:36,460
当你实际取那个互换这两个顶点的变换时（你知道存在这样的变换，因为群的作用是传递的），它具有把一个旋转共轭变换为另一个旋转的效果。
And when you actually take the transformation that switches these two vertices—and you know there is such a transformation, because it permutes them transitively—it has the effect of conjugating one rotation into the other.

143
00:33:36,460 --> 00:33:42,254
在这个细节上你们先相信我。所以事实上，这 20 个元素全都是共轭的。
You have to believe me on that. So that, in fact, these 20 elements are all conjugate.

144
00:33:42,254 --> 00:33:58,380
然而，如果你对 5 阶元素做同样的分析：我们知道这个子群与那个子群共轭，等等。但在该 5 阶子群中，哪些元素实际上彼此共轭呢？
However, if you do the same thing for the elements of order 5: here we know that this subgroup is conjugate to this subgroup, etc. But which elements of this subgroup of order 5 are actually conjugate to each other?

145
00:33:58,380 --> 00:34:06,218
我们只有一种工具可用：我们可以像这样把这个面变到对面，看看它对旋转产生什么影响。
We only have one thing that we can use: we can take this face to this face like that, and see what it does to rotation.

146
00:34:06,218 --> 00:34:11,070
结果表明，当你用它做共轭时，它把一个旋转变成其逆旋转。
And it turns out it takes a rotation into its inverse rotation when you conjugate by that.

147
00:34:11,070 --> 00:34:20,777
因此在每个子群中，元素 g与 g^{-1}（即 g^4）共轭，但与另外两个元素不共轭。
So in each of these subgroups, an element g is conjugate to g^{-1}, which is g^4, but not to these two elements.

148
00:34:20,777 --> 00:34:27,570
所以在每个子群中，有两个元素互相共轭，另外两个元素 g^2 和 g^3 彼此共轭。
So in each one of these subgroups, two elements are conjugate to each other, and two elements, g^2 and g^3, are conjugate to each other.

149
00:34:27,570 --> 00:34:38,730
因此这把 24 个元素的集合分成了两组：在每个群中我们得到两个元素与这里的两个共轭、与这里的两个共轭、与这里的两个共轭、
And so that breaks this set of 24 elements into two sets: in each group we get two that are conjugate to two in here, that are conjugate to two in here, that are conjugate to two in here,

150
00:34:38,730 --> 00:34:49,110
与这里的两个共轭，与这里的两个共轭——一共是 12 个——以及另外 12 个。这就是将这 24 个 5 阶元素拆分成两个大小为 12 的共轭类。
that are conjugate to two in here, that are conjugate into it here—that's 12—and two others. And that's the breakup of these 24 elements of order 5 into two conjugacy classes of size 12.

151
00:34:49,110 --> 00:35:14,206
它们正是绕轴正向或反向旋转五分之一周。所以这一组是旋转角为 ±2π/5 的旋转，而那一组是旋转角为 ±4π/5 的旋转。
And they're the rotations by, you know, just a fifth of the circle in either the positive or negative direction. So this is rotations by ±2π/5, and these are the rotations by ±4π/5.

152
00:35:14,206 --> 00:35:42,135
好，既然如此，我们——现在这个关于作用传递性以及追踪共轭方式的几何论证，给出了类方程，我们看到一共有 5 个大小分别为 1、15、20、12 和 12 的共轭类。
Okay, that being the case, we— now this geometric argument about transitivity of action and following how things conjugate gives us the class equation, and we see that we have five conjugacy classes of size 1, 15, 20, 12, and 12.

153
00:35:42,135 --> 00:36:11,140
把它们全加起来，正好得到 60 个元素。现在想想看——我们接着要证明G 是单群。命题：Gamma 是单群。  证明：设 H 为 Gamma 的非平凡正规子群（H ≠ {e}）。
If you add this all up, you get to 60 elements. Now imagine that—now we're going to prove that G is simple. Proposition: Gamma is a simple group.   Proof: let H be a normal subgroup of Gamma with H not equal to the identity.

154
00:36:11,140 --> 00:36:35,051
那我断言，因为对所有 g 有 g H g^{-1}等于 H——这就是正规子群的定义——所以 H 是 Gamma 中若干个共轭类的并集。
Then I claim, since g H g^{-1} is equal to H for all g—that's the definition of what a normal subgroup is—H is a union of conjugacy classes in Gamma.

155
00:36:35,051 --> 00:36:43,460
如果 H 中包含某个元素，由于该性质，它必须包含其全体共轭元素，同意吧？
If you have one element in H, you have to have all the conjugate elements in H because of this, agreed?

156
00:36:43,460 --> 00:36:55,205
好，那么我必须弄清楚 H 的阶可能是什么。因此我必须挑选上面这些数的一个子集，让它们的和等于H 的阶。
Okay, so then I have to figure out what could be the order of H. So I have to put together a subset of these numbers that adds up to the order of H.

157
00:36:55,205 --> 00:37:02,822
所以 H 的阶等于 1 加上面某些项的和。
So the order of H is equal to 1 plus some of the terms above.

158
00:37:02,822 --> 00:37:22,920
也许它可以是 1加 15，或 1 加 20，或 1 加 12 加 15，诸如此类。但是——关键在于——除了全部项之和以外，这些项的任何组合都不能整除 60！
Maybe it could be 1 plus 15, or 1 plus 20, or 1 plus 12 plus 15, something like that. But—and here's the kicker—no combination of these terms except for all of them divides 60!

159
00:37:22,920 --> 00:37:37,363
唯有全部项加起来才能整除 G 的阶。
Except all terms divides the order of G.

160
00:37:37,363 --> 00:37:52,050
你无法选出一个子集相加得到……这显而易见：一旦你用了 20 和 1，大于 21 的 G 的因子只有 30，对吧？但你凑不出 30。
You can't select a subset and add up to... well, I mean it's pretty clear: once you use 20 and 1, the only divisor of G bigger than 21 is 30, right? So you can't get to 30.

161
00:37:52,050 --> 00:38:03,723
而其他可能的……你知道 60 的因子——60 的较大因子有：30、20，还有什么，15？
And so the other possible... you know that the divisors of 60—you get the big divisors of 60: you got 30, you get 20, and then what, 15?

162
00:38:03,723 --> 00:38:17,591
是的，但我们这里的数必须大于 12，因为它必须是1 加上面某些项，所以至少是 13。因此我们可能考虑的因子只有 15、20和 30。
Yeah, but then we'd have that the number is bigger than 12, because it has to be 1 plus some of the terms above, so it's at least 13. So the only possible divisors we have yet to hit are 15, 20, and 30.

163
00:38:17,591 --> 00:38:20,740
然而无论你怎么组合，都凑不出 15、20 或 30！
And there's no way of putting those together to get 15, 20, or 30!

164
00:38:20,740 --> 00:38:33,890
因此，能够成为共轭类之并且不为平凡群的唯一子群只能是全群。所以它是单群！很漂亮吧？这是一个惊艳的论证。
Therefore, the only subgroup which could be a union of conjugacy classes and is not the identity is the full group. Therefore it's simple! Isn't that nice? It's a striking argument.

165
00:38:33,890 --> 00:38:39,575
通常你并不希望枚举出所有的共轭类，但在本例中我们可以做到。
Usually you don't want to have to enumerate all the conjugacy classes, but in this case we can.

166
00:38:39,575 --> 00:39:09,730
顺便说一句，如果你们当中有人想尝试用交错群的新记号练练身手，用我们的置换记号，  你会发现 g = (1 2 3 4 5) 以及 g' = g^2，
By the way, those of you who want to try your mettle on the new notation for the alternating group, in our notation for permutations,   you'll find that g, which is (1 2 3 4 5), and g', which is g^2,

167
00:39:09,730 --> 00:39:34,829
即 (1 3 5 2 4)，在 S_5 中是共轭的，但在 A_5 中不共轭。  它们正代表了正二十面体群中两个不同的 5 阶共轭类。
which is (1 3 5 2 4), are conjugate in S_5, but not in A_5.   And those represent the two different conjugacy classes of order 5 in the group of the icosahedron.

168
00:39:34,829 --> 00:39:53,780
我们虽然尚未证明正二十面体（或正十二面体）群同构于 A_5，但用置换的语言来说，这里是对称群中两个不同的 5 阶元素；它们都在交错群中，都在 A_5 中，它们在较大的群中共轭，但在较小的群中不共轭。
We haven't yet proved the group of the icosahedron or the dodecahedron is the same as A_5, but in our permutation terms, here are two different elements of order 5 in the symmetric group; they're both in the alternating group, they're both in A_5, they're conjugate in this larger group, but not in the smaller group.

169
00:39:53,780 --> 00:40:13,249
好，让我向大家介绍一点关于有限单群的内容，然后我今天还要用类方程再做一件事。好，有限单群：有限单群的分类是 20 世纪数学中最伟大的传奇之一。
Okay, let me tell you a little bit about finite simple groups, and then I'm going to go on and do one more thing today with the class equation. Okay, so finite simple groups: finite simple groups is one of the great tales of 20th century mathematics.

170
00:40:13,249 --> 00:40:17,175
我们现在拥有全部有限单群的完整列表。这是一个无限列表，但确实是一个完整的列表。
We now have a list of all of them. So it's an infinite list, but it's a list.

171
00:40:17,175 --> 00:40:34,233
它们从 A_5 开始，然后事实证明所有 A_5 之后的交错群也都是单群。我还可以给你们看一些有限单群的其他例子。
So they start out with A_5, and then it turns out that all the alternating groups beyond A_5 are simple. And I can give you some other examples of finite simple groups.

172
00:40:34,233 --> 00:41:00,683
例如取群SL_2(F_p)——即 p 元域上的 2 阶矩阵群，抱歉，行列式为 1 的矩阵群——它本身不是单群，因为它包含单位矩阵与负单位矩阵，而那构成了一个正规子群。
So if you take the group SL_2(F_p)—so those are the 2 by 2 matrices over the field of p elements, sorry, of determinant 1—that's not a simple group, because it contains the identity and minus the identity, and that forms a normal subgroup.

173
00:41:00,683 --> 00:41:12,398
但如果你对其商去该正规子群，对所有不小于 5 的素数 p 它都是单群。
But if you form the quotient by that normal subgroup, it's simple for all primes at least 5.

174
00:41:12,398 --> 00:41:21,735
总有少数低阶情形需要排除。那么这个群的阶是多少？
There are always a couple of low cases that you have to exclude. So what's the order of this group?

175
00:41:21,735 --> 00:41:39,410
我们之前看到 GL_2 的阶等于基的数目，即 (p^2 - 1) 乘以 (p^2 - p)，即 (ℤ/pℤ)^2 的基的数目。
Well, we saw that the order of GL_2 was the number of bases, which was (p^2 - 1) times (p^2 - p), bases of (ℤ/pℤ)^2.

176
00:41:39,410 --> 00:41:57,356
而 SL_2 是该群中由行列式为 1 的元素构成的子群。行列式映射将群 GL_2(ℤ/pℤ)满射到 (ℤ/pℤ)^× 上。
And SL_2 is a subgroup of this group consisting of the elements of determinant 1. The determinant maps the group GL_2(ℤ/pℤ) surjectively onto (ℤ/pℤ)^×.

177
00:41:57,356 --> 00:42:09,716
你可以找到具有任何非零行列式的矩阵；即具有非零行列式的元素，而该目标群的阶为 p - 1，对吧？
You can find a matrix of any non-zero determinant; that means the elements of non-zero determinant, and this group has order p - 1, right?

178
00:42:09,716 --> 00:42:21,746
有 p - 1 个非零元素。所以该映射的核（即 SL_2）的阶等于GL_2 的阶除以 p - 1。
There are p - 1 non-zero elements. So the kernel of this map, which is SL_2, has order equal to the order of GL_2 divided by p - 1.

179
00:42:21,746 --> 00:42:28,010
因此 SL_2 的阶就是 (p^2 - 1) · p，因为如果我把这项除以 p - 1 就得到 p。
So the order of this group SL_2 is (p^2 - 1) · p, because if I divide this by p - 1, I just get p.

180
00:42:28,010 --> 00:42:49,605
然后我们要的不是 SL_2，而是要商去这个 2 阶子群，所以这个群 PSL_2(F_p) 的阶就是 p(p^2 - 1) / 2，明白吗？顺便说一句，交错群的阶是 n阶乘除以 2。
And then I don't want SL_2, but I want to divide out by this subgroup of order 2, so the order of this group is (p^2 - 1) · p divided by 2, okay? The order of this group, by the way, is n factorial over 2.

181
00:42:49,605 --> 00:43:03,890
我们来计算其中几个看看能得到什么：对于 p = 5，得到 5 乘以 24 除以 2，即 5 乘以12，所以对于 p = 5 这个群的阶为 60！
So let's compute a few of these just to see what we get: for p = 5, I get 5 times 24 over 2, 5 times 12, so this group has order 60 for p = 5!

182
00:43:03,890 --> 00:43:27,256
你可能不会感到意外，它同构于这个群：该群阶为 60，下一个群阶为 360。好，下一项 p = 7 呢？群的阶等于 7 乘以 48除以 2，即 7 乘以 24，等于 168。
And you might not be surprised to find out that it's isomorphic to this group: this group has order 60, this group has order 360. Okay, what about the next case, p = 7? The group has order 7 times 48 over 2, 7 times 24, which is 168.

183
00:43:27,256 --> 00:43:38,649
这正是第二小的非交换单群：168！所以这里有一条无限的单群链，这里有另一条无限链，对吧？
That turns out to be the next smallest non-abelian simple group: 168! So here's an infinite chain of simple groups, here's another infinite chain, okay?

184
00:43:38,649 --> 00:43:53,386
所以在 20 世纪初，数学家们开始构造这些无限链并发现越来越多的有限单群，最终他们找到了一套通法。
So mathematicians at the beginning of the 20th century began to make these infinite chains and find more and more finite simple groups, and eventually they produced a method.

185
00:43:53,386 --> 00:44:04,950
有一位伟大的数学家叫克劳德·谢瓦莱（Claude Chevalley），他在 1950 年代末提出了一种方法，构造出整整一系列这种类型的群：
There was a great mathematician named Claude Chevalley who at the end of the 1950s came up with a method to produce a whole list of groups of this type:

186
00:44:04,950 --> 00:44:13,950
它们被称为李型有限单群，因为它们源于李型群。你可以对 SL_3 和 SL_4 也做同样的事，我应该顺便提一下。好。
they're called finite groups of Lie type, because they're Lie-type groups. So you can also do this for SL_3 and SL_4, I should tell you that, okay.

187
00:44:13,950 --> 00:44:28,169
人们想知道这个列表是否完备，但它并不完备，因为在 19 世纪中叶，一位名叫马修（Mathieu）的法国数学家曾描述过四个相当奇特的置换群，
And people wondered whether that list was complete, and it wasn't complete, because in the middle of the 19th century a French mathematician by the name of Mathieu had described four rather bizarre permutation

188
00:44:28,169 --> 00:44:36,509
称为马修群。它们分别置换 11 个字母、12 个字母、23 个字母和 24 个字母。
groups called the Mathieu groups. They permuted 11 letters, and 12 letters, and 23 letters, and 24 letters.

189
00:44:36,509 --> 00:44:42,248
它们是 S_11、S_12 等群的子群，并不在谢瓦莱的列表中，所以它们被称为散在单群。
So they were subgroups of S_11 and S_12 which were not on Chevalley's list, so those were called sporadic groups.

190
00:44:42,248 --> 00:44:51,825
然后大家以为差不多找齐了，结果计算机又发现了一个散在单群，接着人们开始在计算机上发现更多的散在单群，直到最终找到了我上次跟你们讲过的那个被称为魔群（Monster group）的群，
And then everyone thought they were about done, and then the computer discovered another sporadic group, and then they started discovering other sporadic groups on the computer, until they finally found that group I told you about last time,

191
00:44:51,825 --> 00:45:03,315
它的阶大约是 10 的 54 次方（或 10 的 47 次方）——它其实并不是直接在计算机上找到的，你根本无法把那个群写出来，但它的共轭类在某种意义上是在计算机上被理解的。
called the Monster group, which has order 10 to the 47th—and it really wasn't discovered on the computer, you can't write that group down, but its conjugacy classes were in some sense understood on the computer.

192
00:45:03,315 --> 00:45:19,560
最近——所谓最近，我是指 10 年前——数学界证明了谢瓦莱发现的李型群列表，加上主要在计算机辅助下发现的 26 个散在单群，构成了有限单群的完整分类。
And recently—and when I mean recently, I mean 10 years ago—it was proved that the lists of groups that Chevalley had discovered plus 26 sporadic groups that had been basically discovered on the computer comprised the full list of finite simple groups.

193
00:45:19,560 --> 00:45:29,561
这是我们这个世纪数学最伟大的胜利之一。下次我会带一本书来给你们看，叫《有限群图集》（ATLAS of Finite Groups），里面给出了关于有限单群的各种信息。
It's one of the great triumphs of our century in mathematics. I'm going to bring you in a book next time called the ATLAS of Finite Groups, which gives all kinds of information about the finite simple groups.

194
00:45:29,561 --> 00:45:34,090
不可能给出全部，因为它们有无穷多个——你甚至无法给出关于交错群的全部信息。
You can't give more, because there's an infinite number—you couldn't even give all the information about the alternating groups.

195
00:45:34,090 --> 00:45:49,539
但它给出足够多交错群的信息，让你能看出总体规律，同样也给出了这一链条中足够多的群。所以你们现在知道了最小的有限单群。
But what it does is it gives information about enough alternating groups so you start to see the general pattern, and likewise enough in this chain. So you now know the first finite simple group.

196
00:45:49,539 --> 00:45:55,165
上次我向大家证明了，如果一个群的阶是素数幂，它必然具有非平凡中心。
Now last time I showed you that if you had a group of prime power order, it had a non-trivial center.

197
00:45:55,165 --> 00:46:01,929
我要回顾一下那个结论，并且再讲一件事，今天就结束。
So I'm going to recall that, and do one more thing, and we're done today.

198
00:46:07,579 --> 00:46:23,707
G 的中心 Z(G) 不等于平凡单位元。证明如下：考虑类方程。
The center of G is not equal to the identity element. And the proof goes like this: consider the class equation.

199
00:46:23,707 --> 00:46:47,319
G 的阶（即 p^n）等于1（单位元的共轭类的阶）加上各项 |G|/|Z(g)| 的和，其中 g 遍历不等于单位元的各个共轭类代表元。
The order of G, which is p^n, is equal to 1—the order of the conjugacy class of the identity—plus the sum of the order of G over the centralizer of g, for g not equal to the identity, conjugacy classes.

200
00:46:48,499 --> 00:47:28,289
因此如果所有这些数都……如果对所有 g ≠ e，Z(g) 都不等于 G，那么 |G| 除以|Z(g)| 对所有这些项都能被 p 整除，因为分子是 p 的某个幂次，分母是 p 的某个更小的幂次，所以商保留了能被 p 整除的 p 的方幂。
So if all of these numbers are... if Z(g) is not equal to G for all g not equal to the identity, then the order of G over the order of Z(g) is divisible by p for all these terms, because this is some power of p, this is some smaller power of p, so you're left with a power of p dividing the quotient.

201
00:47:28,289 --> 00:47:46,583
但这是荒谬的，因为那意味着 p^n 等于 1 加上一个能被 p 整除的数，因为若干个能被 p 整除的数的和自身也能被 p 整除。
But that's ridiculous, because that would say that p^n is 1 plus a number divisible by p, because the sum of numbers divisible by p is itself divisible by p.

202
00:47:46,583 --> 00:47:54,600
这是荒谬的：这项能被 p 整除，这项也能被p 整除，而它除以 p 的余数却是 1！所以这是一个矛盾。
And that's ridiculous: this is divisible by p, this is divisible by p, this has remainder 1 when divided by p! So that's a contradiction.

203
00:47:54,600 --> 00:48:17,750
因此，至少有一项的中心化子的阶必须等于 G 的阶，这样的元素落在中心里，即对某个非单位元 g 有 Z(g) = G，因此 g 落在中心中。
Consequently, one of these terms at least has to have the order of the centralizer equal to the order of G, and such an element is in the center, and Z(g) is equal to G for some g not equal to the identity, and g is therefore in the center.

204
00:48:17,750 --> 00:48:47,643
所以素数幂阶群的中心是非平凡的。让我们把这个结论再推进一步。推论：若 G 的阶等于 p，则 G 是循环群；若 G 的阶等于 p^2，则 G 必为交换群！
So the center of a group of prime power order is non-trivial. Let's push that a little harder. Corollary: if the order of G is equal to p, G is cyclic; if the order of G is equal to p^2, G is abelian!

205
00:48:47,643 --> 00:48:51,638
所以对于较小的 p 的方幂，我们能说得更多：整个群内部元素彼此对易。
So for small powers of p, we can say more than it has a center: the whole group commutes with itself.

206
00:48:51,638 --> 00:49:12,595
我们之前已经证明了这点：如果你有一个p 阶群，取任何非单位元，它都能生成整个群——由任何 g ≠ e 生成，这是已知的。所以现在我们只需证明交换群这个结论。
Well, we've already done this: if you have a group of order p, and you take any non-identity element, it generates the group—generated by any g not equal to the identity, that we know. So now we have to prove this abelian business.

207
00:49:12,595 --> 00:49:38,581
它具有非平凡中心。证明：G 的中心 Z(G) 不等于平凡单位元，所以其阶为 p 或 p^2，因为这是我们就证完了，对吧？
Well, it has a non-trivial center. Proof: the center of G is not equal to the identity, so has order p or p^2, because those are we are done, correct?

208
00:49:38,581 --> 00:49:47,431
因为如果中心的阶为 p^2，这意味着一切元素都彼此对易，我们就证完了。
Because if the center has order p^2, that says everything commutes with everything, we're done.

209
00:49:47,431 --> 00:50:31,950
如果不是，若G 的中心的阶为 p，取 G 中一个不属于中心的元素 g，  考虑该元素 g 的中心化子G 的中心的阶为 p，取 G 中一个不属于中心的元素 g，考虑该元素 g 的中心化子元素 g 自身，因为 g 与自身对易，
If not, if the center of G has order p, take an element in G which is not in the center,   and consider the centralizer of the element center of G has order p, take an element in G which is not in the center, and consider the centralizer of the element element g, because g commutes with itself,

210
00:50:31,950 --> 00:50:50,114
所以该子群严格大于中心，明白吗？  如果该群严格更大，它的阶现在必须是 p^2。如果这个元素 g 自身，因为 g 与自身对易，所以该子群严格大于中心，明白吗？如果该群严格更大，它的阶现在必须是 p^2。
and this group is strictly larger than the center, okay?   Well, if this group is strictly larger, this now has order p^2. If this element g, because g commutes with itself, and this group is strictly larger than the center, okay? Well, if this group is strictly larger, this now has order p^2.

211
00:50:50,114 --> 00:51:02,084
如果这个群的阶为 p^2，那它就是全群，这蕴含了 g 属于 G 的中心，因为它的中心化子是整个群。
If this group has order p^2, that's the whole group, which implies that g is in the center of G, because its centralizer is the entire group.

212
00:51:02,084 --> 00:51:11,935
但这与 g 不在 G 的中心这一事实矛盾！因此中心阶为 p 的假设是不可能的。
But that contradicts the fact that g was not in the center of G! So the hypothesis that the center had order p is impossible.

213
00:51:11,935 --> 00:51:15,510
所以中心的阶必须是 p^2，证毕！
So therefore the center has order p^2, and we're done!

214
00:51:15,510 --> 00:51:29,208
现在你可能会想，因为我还没给你们看过反例，素数幂阶群是否总是交换群？也许这个定理很弱，也许任何p^3 阶群也都是交换群？
Now you might think, because I haven't shown you otherwise, that a group of prime power order is always abelian. Maybe this is very weak, maybe any group of order p^3 is abelian?

215
00:51:29,208 --> 00:51:35,988
所以为了向大家展示这是一个真正有意义的好定理，我必须向大家展示一个非交换的 p^3 阶群。
So to show you that this is a good theorem that is actually meaningful, I have to show you a group of order p^3 that's not abelian.

216
00:51:35,988 --> 00:52:03,997
它在这里：一个 p^3 阶非交换群。取 G 为 GL_3(F_p) 的子群。瞧，我们有了这些矩阵群是多么有用！它是由形如这样的矩阵构成的群。
So here it is: a non-abelian group of order p^3. Take G a subgroup of GL_3(F_p). See, it's so useful now that we have these matrix groups! And it's the group consisting of the matrices that look like this.

217
00:52:03,997 --> 00:52:19,233
我断言它是一个子群，因为如果你把这种矩阵相乘，得到的形式依然相同，它在乘法和求逆运算下封闭。
I claim that's a subgroup, because if you multiply matrices like this you get another one, it's closed under multiplication and inversion.

218
00:52:19,233 --> 00:52:43,789
它的阶显然是 p^3，因为x 有 p 种选择，y 有 p 种选择，z 有 p 种选择。你可以通过乘法验证它是非交换的。事实上，G 的中心阶为 p，且由 x 和 y 均为 0 的矩阵构成。
You know it's clearly order p^3, because you have p choices for x, p choices for y, and p choices for z, and you can check by multiplication it's non-abelian. In fact, the center of G has order p, and consists of the matrices that look like this where x and y are both zero.

219
00:52:43,789 --> 00:52:49,247
这是一个很好的习题，去观察一个 p^3 阶非交换群。
That's a good exercise to see a non-abelian group of order p^3.

220
00:52:49,247 --> 00:53:06,660
但你看，这个论证说明中心不能是 p^2 阶，因为如果中心具有p^2 阶，我们在这里用同样的论证就能证明全群都是中心。所以在这里，如果它不是 p^2 阶，但它非平凡，就必须是 p 阶。
But you see, this argument shows the center couldn't have order p^2, because if the center had order p^2, we'd do the same argument here and show that the whole group was the center. So here, if it's not going to have order p^2, but it's non-trivial, it has to have order p.

221
00:53:06,660 --> 00:53:14,220
这就是一个中心为 p 阶的 p^3 阶非交换群的例子。很好，我们现在真正深入到了实质内容。
Here's an example of a non-abelian group of order p^3 where the center has order p. Good, so we're really getting into the real stuff now.

222
00:53:14,220 --> 00:53:23,429
很快我们就会真正掌握如何在对称群中进行运算。祝大家周末愉快！
Pretty soon we'll actually know how to work in the symmetric group. Have a nice weekend!
